 take so many of  those before you're not going to be able  to get up how concerned is he that he's  taking too much physical abuse the way  that he plays the game  well i even posed a question to him mike  and it's something that you're a witness  to i said  i sit next to uh in our sunday screening  room for football in america tony gunty  on my left rodney harrison on my right  and at some point any one of the three  of us say  man this kid's gonna get hurt he can't  he can't take all these hits so lamar's  like hey i can i'm okay he's like i'm  smart about it too  he's he's being smart about getting  himself out of bounds getting himself  down but he feels like the way he's  built and for whatever reason i don't  know if it's our memories of him when he  won the heisman at louisville  he has a look he looks a little slighter  slighter than he is he is thick uh he  he's tall he's 6-1 he's powerful  and he has that in him so he feels like  he can take that kind of  extra hits that other quarterbacks  aren't getting guys who are pure pocket  passers and still be okay but he also  sees his game as evolving as to not just  being a runner but being a complete  quarterback so when i asked him directly  he said i'm good i can do this i can get  through this i'm not taking too many  hits so time will answer that question  but that's where his mind is and  look we'll see sunday what do the  patriots do best better than anybody in  the modern nfl they take away what you  do best what the ravens do best is lamar  jackson running so will they make lamar  jackson throw the ball to win the game  can they get to that point that'll be  the fascinating thing to watch on sunday  night  and there's a very healthy amount of  dislike between the ravens and the  patriots is the first time lamar  jackson's going to see the patriots did  you get the impression that he's gotten  the memo that this is one of the teams  that the ravens collectively hate  i i'm sure that's easy to figure out  just by being around baltimore i'm sure  he's got that i will say this he has as  you would imagine immense respect for  tom brady and looking up tom brady and  calling the goat and all that mike i  think he had the sound bite slash quote  of the first half of the season for me  he said tom brady when he's in the  pocket it's like he's on vacation  and he talks about wanting to be that  calm in the pocket and now just think of  that visual i love it and that's where  the kid's aspiring to go so it gives you  a mindset of where he's going forward  but also a little bit of his personality  as well he's just pure honest uh very  very likable young man and i i hope that  we continue to see him grow because look  these are as you were alluding to  earlier with mayfield and rosen and all  the other guys and all these drafts that  these these are the feature quarterbacks  of the week and we saw garoppolo play  well last night and kyler murray every  time we watch kyler murray go okay you  know what's getting better getting  better getting better  this is where the league is going it's  an exciting group of young men and  lamar's right there in the middle of it  yeah and lamar's right in the middle of  the mvp conversation and i'd say he's  one of the three or four leading  candidates right now mike he has to keep  doing what he's done he has to stay  healthy but  he and you know and they never really  give you a definition of what mvp means  but when you look at value to the ravens  if we're gonna if we're gonna base it on  value to your team it is clear that this  ravens team wouldn't be anywhere close  to five and two without him  it's it's a great conversation to get  people  sparked and inspired make him do a  deeper dive mike uh seven yards just  under seven yards per carry average  his before contact yardage before  anybody touches him speed ability play  design is 4.2 yards that's what the  league averages per run so he's getting  the league average before anybody  touches him  great pro football focus numbers on  lamar jackson that they give you that  insight he's 10th in the league in  rushing his passer rating is higher than  phillip rivers he's in the middle of the  pack so if you get a guy who could be  top 10 in rushing and top 12 or 14 and  passer rating all rolled into one  yeah you're right with an 11-win team  that would garner  mvp conversation and i think important  night two for the ravens mike at home  against the patriots obviously the  patriots are undefeated the steelers  have a tough game against indianapolis  they didn't set the world up fire in the  first part of the game against miami  they are home for indy but if indy a  good team goes in there and beats  pittsburgh and baltimore has a chance to  take a three-game lead  in the loss column  on the steelers  that would be significant all of a  sudden if if pittsburgh wins at home and  then the patriots beat baltimore now  this division race becomes tight for the  second half of the season i think a very  pivotal week here for the ravens in the  nfc the afcc uh north north of race  hey mike and let's broaden it just a  little bit as well because the ravens  are a serious contender to be the number  two seed in the afc and get the bye week  that goes along with it with the chiefs  now  at five and three  patrick mahomes who knows what's gonna  happen with him will we see him this  sunday if he doesn't play this sunday  they lose the vikings they fall to five  and four you start to get separation  there and it could be the ravens two  seed patriots one seed and if the ravens  would happen to win sunday night they  can start thinking about possibly being  the one seed  that's a long way away but you're right  when you start thinking of it that way  and same through the winter of the afc  south  they're also going to be that  conversation for the two seed as well i  think the kansas city thing is really  fascinating already three losses at home  uh a team you know so well the vikings  coming into town to play them at  arrowhead it could be possible that  through half the season plus nine weeks  that kansas city could have four home  losses that would be stunning stuff but  it is a possibility and you start to  look back okay have they beaten anybody  at home yeah they beat baltimore at home  so they they hold that for tiebreaker  purposes but i think while the matchups  may not be super sexy here these couple  of games that minnesota kansas city game  the sunday night game  are going to have a long way to  determining how the afc shakes out when  we uh when we get done with this  let's flip it over to the nfc in the  last minute or two that i have you here  who do you think the best team in that  conference is right now  i can make a really good argument in my  head for  all three of the group of san francisco  new orleans  and green bay  if you start to ask me i know i'm trying  to take the recency bias away just  having watched san francisco where their  defense maybe gave you a little bit of a  question of their dominance by giving up  25 to arizona  but your questions about jimmy garoppolo  i think are eased after you watch the  way he played last night so  let's keep san francisco where they  where you thought they were before the  thursday night game  that new orleans defensive front is  terrific and right now with brees back  healthy coming off a bye this week going  into you know arrested and healthy herb  breeze  i like the way new orleans stacks up for  the second half of the season i think  because of the difficulty of the nfc  north would be a little bit tougher for  green bay to get to the top  so that's dancing around the question i  think if he had forced me for an answer  right now i would begrudgingly give you  new orleans but i would say uh  incomplete would be the great there i  think we need to see the second half of  the season  it is going to be a heck of a scramble  in the nfc for playoff spots for bye  weeks for the number one seed because  you don't want to go to new orleans in  january you don't want to go to lambeau  field in january san francisco is going  to want to be right at home and force  those teams to come to them all right my  great stuff the lamar jackson interview  available on the mike trico podcast and  the nbc sports youtube channel at  youtube.com nbc sports mike thanks for  some of your time on a friday morning  enjoy notre dame and virginia tech  tomorrow and we'll see you sunday for  football night in america  see you bright and early sunday morning  mike thanks have a great weekend pal  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

